            'eligibility_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Sponsor Requirements</h4><p>For the permanent-residence route, the sponsor must be a Barbadian citizen (including by origin or descent). For the less formal dependant permission, the sponsor is a lawful resident holding a valid work permit.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Who Qualifies</h4><ul><li>Person married to a Barbadian citizen</li><li>Resident married to a citizen by origin or descent</li><li>Person who has been married to, and cohabited with, a Barbadian citizen for a "prescribed period" before applying</li><li>For work-permit holders: spouse and minor children</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>CARICOM Note</h4><p>A separate citizenship-registration route exists for CARICOM nationals and their spouses — not directly relevant to Indian ordinary-passport holders unless they also hold CARICOM nationality.</p>',
            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Entry to Barbados — Conflicting Information</h4><p>Our research found conflicting evidence on whether Indian citizens currently need a visa to enter Barbados. A 2021 Indian High Commission advisory and Barbados tourism authority notice stated a visa requirement was imposed in May 2021 (described at the time as a temporary, COVID-related measure, "until further notice"), with a reported ~10 working day processing time and a single-entry fee of approximately US$107. A more recent-looking but unofficial aggregator (Skyscanner) states no visa is needed. We could not resolve this conflict and recommend checking directly with the Barbados Ministry of Foreign Affairs or the nearest Barbadian mission before travel.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Documents for the Family-Based Route</h4><p>Expect to need your marriage certificate and proof of cohabitation (if applicable) for the permanent-residence-via-marriage route; exact document checklists were not independently confirmed.</p>',
