            'intro_html' => '<p>Bolivia does not appear to have one single named "family visa." Based on available evidence, a foreign spouse or minor child of someone holding Bolivian temporary residence (Permanencia Temporal) can typically apply for their own Permanencia Temporal on family-reunion grounds, via a specific-purpose entry visa (visa de objeto determinado) followed by registration with Bolivia\'s immigration authority. After a period of continuous temporary residence (commonly cited as around 2 years, not independently confirmed), the holder may become eligible for Permanencia Definitiva (permanent residence). A separate refugee family-reunification channel exists via CONARE, but this applies only to persons already recognised as refugees in Bolivia and is not the general route for an Indian family seeking to reunite.</p>',
