            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Thin Official Information</h4><p>We were unable to confirm, via available search sources, a dedicated official process description for Indian citizens applying for family reunification or a family visit to the Central African Republic. What follows is drawn from secondary guides only.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>If You Are the Applicant</h4><ul><li>Marriage certificate (for spouse) or birth certificate (for dependent children)</li><li>Copies of the sponsor\'s CAR work and residence permit</li><li>Medical certificate (for dependents, per one secondary source)</li><li>Police clearance certificate (for adult dependents, per one secondary source)</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>If You Are the Sponsor</h4><p>You would need to already hold a valid CAR work and residence permit and show proof of financial support before dependents can apply.</p><p>Given the sparse official documentation, we strongly recommend direct confirmation with the Central African Republic embassy/consulate or Ministry of Foreign Affairs before proceeding, and our consultants can help coordinate that outreach.</p>',
