            'official_visa_name' => 'Visa de Beneficiario (Beneficiary Visa, tied to a Visa M or Visa R principal holder)',
            'visa_subclass_code' => 'M (beneficiary dependent on principal M/R visa)',
            'intro_html' => '<p>Colombia has a formally documented, officially confirmed beneficiary/dependent visa provision under Resolucion 5477 de 2022 (as amended), administered by the Cancilleria (Ministry of Foreign Affairs). A Visa de Beneficiario can be requested by the spouse or permanent partner (compañero/a permanente) and by children under 25 who are economically dependent on a principal Visa M or Visa R holder (children over 25 can qualify if a qualified disability prevents financial independence). Importantly, the Cancilleria\'s own list of principal visas that can sponsor a beneficiary is narrow among Visa V (short/medium-stay visitor visa) subcategories -- it names only V Estudiante (postgraduate only), V Religioso, V Voluntario o Cooperante, V Nomada Digital, and V Corresponsal Permanente. A general Visa V (e.g. ordinary visitor/tourism) does NOT appear on this list, so it should not be assumed to allow sponsoring a beneficiary.</p>',
