            'eligibility_html' => '<p>One aggregator describes the Family Reunification route as open to all nationalities, ages 18-99, under Law No. 88-025 on residence conditions for foreigners in Comoros. No source confirmed specific eligible relationships (spouse vs. unmarried partner vs. children) in any detail, nor dependent-child age limits -- these remain unconfirmed.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Caution on a Separate Marriage-Based Claim</h4><p>A lower-reliability source describes acquiring Comorian citizenship through marriage to a citizen (not a residence permit), with figures (a KMF 20,000 minimum annual salary, an 18-21 age range) that look internally inconsistent and were not corroborated elsewhere -- we do not treat this as reliable guidance.</p><p>Given sparse official publication, treat all details here as indicative only pending direct confirmation from Comorian authorities.</p>',
            'indian_applicant_html' => '<h4 style=\'margin:0 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>Visa Requirement Itself Is Unclear</h4><p>Search sources conflict on whether Indian citizens need a visa for Comoros at all -- some describe visa-free or visa-on-arrival entry for up to 45 days, others say a visa is required in advance and that no e-visa is available to Indian passport holders. This conflict should be resolved by contacting the Comoros Embassy/Honorary Consulate or an airline before travel.</p><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>If Relocating to Join Family</h4><ul><li>Apply for a long-stay visa (specific document list not independently confirmed)</li><li>Once in Comoros, apply to the Ministry of Interior for a residence card under the Family Reunification provision</li><li>Expect to renew the residence card annually</li></ul><h4 style=\'margin:20px 0 10px;font-size:16px;\'>If Only Visiting Family</h4><p>This would likely fall under whichever short-stay/visa-on-arrival rules currently apply to Indian citizens -- confirm current status directly, since sources conflict.</p><p>Given how thin official Comorian documentation is, we strongly recommend direct verification with the Comoros Embassy/Honorary Consulate in New Delhi or Comoros\'s Ministry of Interior before relying on this guidance; our consultants can help with that outreach.</p>',
