            'intro_html' => '<p>Croatia is a full EU and Schengen member (since 1 January 2023), so a short family VISIT by an Indian national generally runs through the ordinary Schengen short-stay (Type C) visa, applied for at a Croatian consulate or an authorised visa centre in India, with an invitation letter and relationship proof supporting the application. For a LONGER stay to live with a family member in Croatia, Croatia runs its own national route, Temporary Stay for the Purpose of Family Reunification, under the Aliens Act — this is separate from the Schengen visit visa and is not automatically granted just because a relative lives in Croatia.</p>',
