            'intro_html' => '<p>Curacao is a constituent country of the Kingdom of the Netherlands with its own entry rules, distinct from the European Netherlands/Schengen area. Per prior project research, Indian nationals generally need a Dutch Caribbean short-stay visa, processed via the Netherlands Embassy/Consulate, for a short family VISIT. For a LONGER stay to live with a family member who is a Curacao resident, Curacao runs a separate national route — the Rib\'e Lugá program, which issues a temporary residence permit to dependent family members for the purpose of family reunification or family formation. These are two different processes and should not be conflated.</p>',
            'typical_stay' => 'Short-stay visit: sources conflict, citing figures between 15 and 90 days (Netherlands Worldwide cites up to 30 consecutive days, with longer stays up to 90 days needing in-country extension approval). Rib\'e Lugá residence permit: duration tied to the sponsor\'s own permit, and since 1 April 2026 cannot exceed the sponsor\'s (main applicant\'s) permit validity.',
            'entry_type' => 'Short visit: Dutch Caribbean short-stay visa (not valid for the European Netherlands or Schengen). Reunification: national temporary residence permit via Rib\'e Lugá, requiring an approved sponsor already in Curacao.',
