            'intro_html' => '<p>Cyprus is an EU member since 2004 but, per this project\'s earlier research, is NOT YET a Schengen member — officials have targeted 2026 for accession but no confirmed entry date was found, so Schengen family-visa rules do not apply and Cyprus runs its own national family routes under the Aliens and Immigration Law. Two distinct tracks were found: (1) formal Family Reunification for the spouse and minor children of a third-country national who is already a long-settled Cyprus resident, and (2) a dependent-permit route attached to the "Pink Slip" temporary residence permit held by financially self-sufficient (non-working) residents. These are different sponsor categories with different conditions.</p>',
